1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,350
This video summarizes
the complete Foundry lab,

2
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,697
starting from a new Azure resource group.

3
00:00:05,957 --> 00:00:09,618
It replays records of actual
commands and managed-service results,

4
00:00:09,618 --> 00:00:12,647
not a recording of the separately
authenticated portal.

5
00:00:12,907 --> 00:00:15,398
A fictional Contoso
support Agent retrieves

6
00:00:15,398 --> 00:00:17,626
policies and answers twelve questions.

7
00:00:17,886 --> 00:00:20,109
v1 starts deliberately plain.

8
00:00:20,369 --> 00:00:24,253
You evaluate it, let
Agent Optimizer propose changes,

9
00:00:24,253 --> 00:00:26,785
review them by hand, and compare v2.

10
00:00:27,045 --> 00:00:29,280
This lab does not retrain model weights.

11
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:34,751
First inspect the signed-in Azure CLI
user, tenant and subscription.

12
00:00:35,011 --> 00:00:37,468
A successful sign-in
alone does not establish

13
00:00:37,468 --> 00:00:39,924
that the correct lab
environment is selected.

14
00:00:40,184 --> 00:00:42,955
The portal and the CLI
authenticate separately;

15
00:00:42,955 --> 00:00:47,212
check both, and never bypass personal
authentication or switch accounts.

16
00:00:47,472 --> 00:00:50,949
Set the language and artifact
directory in every new terminal,

17
00:00:50,949 --> 00:00:52,917
and never mix the two language runs.

18
00:00:53,177 --> 00:00:55,984
In this run, the preflight
record shows the user,

19
00:00:55,984 --> 00:00:58,448
tenant and subscription matched the plan.

20
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:02,152
The plan command creates
local configuration

21
00:01:02,152 --> 00:01:04,433
and an unapproved authorization example.

22
00:01:04,693 --> 00:01:08,220
Check subscription, models,
region and retention first.

23
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:11,900
Sol serves the Agent,
Luna judges the responses,

24
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:15,821
and GPT-5.5 handles optimization
and search planning.

25
00:01:16,081 --> 00:01:19,481
Start with 100,000 TPM
per generative deployment

26
00:01:19,481 --> 00:01:22,719
and 10,000 for embeddings,
in North Central US.

27
00:01:22,979 --> 00:01:28,021
Verify the deployed token limit; do not
assume a universal capacity conversion.

28
00:01:28,281 --> 00:01:30,860
Confirm authorization before provisioning;

29
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:33,572
a local budget entry does
not stop Azure billing.

30
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:38,718
Apply the authorized plan to create
the Foundry account and project,

31
00:01:38,718 --> 00:01:41,218
model deployments, Search and monitoring.

32
00:01:41,478 --> 00:01:43,737
An accepted request is not readiness:

33
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:48,256
inspect the owned-resource status
and confirm all five runtime TPM checks.

34
00:01:48,516 --> 00:01:51,073
Here the manifest reports phase succeeded

35
00:01:51,073 --> 00:01:54,056
with 25 owned entries,
and all five checks passed.

36
00:01:54,316 --> 00:01:59,529
The first attempt hit a CLI timeout, so
status was inspected before apply resumed.

37
00:01:59,789 --> 00:02:02,970
Default monitoring may add
an alert rule and action group;

38
00:02:02,970 --> 00:02:04,722
here only the alert rule exists.

39
00:02:04,982 --> 00:02:07,360
Never adopt or delete
a shared action group.

40
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,963
The model smoke command checks
one short, real response.

41
00:02:12,223 --> 00:02:15,199
This confirms connectivity,
not answer quality.

42
00:02:15,459 --> 00:02:18,779
Next upload the eight
language-matched synthetic policies,

43
00:02:18,779 --> 00:02:22,673
and prepare the search index, knowledge
base and read-only connection.

44
00:02:22,933 --> 00:02:25,816
Do not confuse creation
with successful retrieval.

45
00:02:26,076 --> 00:02:28,213
Confirm real references in the probe,

46
00:02:28,213 --> 00:02:31,953
and separately verify access under
the Agent's managed identity.

47
00:02:32,213 --> 00:02:35,991
In this run the smoke call completed,
eight policies were uploaded,

48
00:02:35,991 --> 00:02:38,907
and the probe returned five
real policy references.

49
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:43,308
Create the fixed v1 Agent
with its policy tool.

50
00:02:43,568 --> 00:02:46,622
An identical configuration
is verified and reused;

51
00:02:46,622 --> 00:02:49,330
changes to tools
or permissions are rejected.

52
00:02:49,590 --> 00:02:53,039
This v1 is deliberately
plain: one short sentence,

53
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:56,409
and never calculate dates,
deadlines or amounts.

54
00:02:56,669 --> 00:02:58,662
That leaves visible room for improvement.

55
00:02:58,922 --> 00:03:02,134
Send the guide's example
question and inspect answer,

56
00:03:02,134 --> 00:03:04,159
citations, route and needs human.

57
00:03:04,419 --> 00:03:08,287
Verify the real policy-tool
call and document identifiers.

58
00:03:08,547 --> 00:03:12,265
Valid JSON alone does
not establish policy correctness.

59
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,508
Use the guide's dev12
JSONL without editing it,

60
00:03:16,508 --> 00:03:21,049
verify its row count and hash,
then register the first dataset version.

61
00:03:21,309 --> 00:03:23,903
A five-row preview does
not mean the dataset

62
00:03:23,903 --> 00:03:26,146
has only five items; check all twelve.

63
00:03:26,406 --> 00:03:29,591
Query is the Agent's input;
context and ground truth

64
00:03:29,591 --> 00:03:32,052
are reference material, not input text.

65
00:03:32,312 --> 00:03:37,100
Editing the file, or embedding its answers
in instructions, breaks the comparison.

66
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:41,724
This run registered lab-en-dev12,
version one, with twelve rows.

67
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:47,263
An evaluator defines what to score;
the Judge model performs the scoring.

68
00:03:47,523 --> 00:03:50,713
Relevance passes at four
or above on a five-point scale.

69
00:03:50,973 --> 00:03:54,879
Task Adherence is binary: one
is a pass, not a low score.

70
00:03:55,139 --> 00:03:58,367
Relevance uses response
text, while Task Adherence

71
00:03:58,367 --> 00:04:02,036
receives output items
with conversation and tool context.

72
00:04:02,296 --> 00:04:06,358
This run uses Relevance version 15
and Task Adherence version 18,

73
00:04:06,358 --> 00:04:08,353
with the Luna Judge deployment.

74
00:04:08,613 --> 00:04:11,313
Confirm the saved mappings
and the actual Judge,

75
00:04:11,313 --> 00:04:14,014
and never move thresholds
after seeing results.

76
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:19,159
Review the dataset and criteria,
then submit the baseline once;

77
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:21,772
steps four through six are one evaluation.

78
00:04:22,032 --> 00:04:24,435
All twelve items completed with no errors.

79
00:04:24,695 --> 00:04:28,399
Nine passed both criteria;
Relevance passed 10,

80
00:04:28,399 --> 00:04:32,013
Task Adherence 11, and mean
Relevance was 3.75.

81
00:04:32,273 --> 00:04:34,944
That is lower on purpose:
v1 is a deliberately

82
00:04:34,944 --> 00:04:37,473
plain starting point with room to improve.

83
00:04:37,733 --> 00:04:41,560
Completed means processing ended,
not that every answer is correct.

84
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:45,183
Record the evaluation and run
IDs with the read-only lookup;

85
00:04:45,183 --> 00:04:47,688
never resubmit just
because the wait is long.

86
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:52,469
Connect each answer and scoring
reason to the source policy;

87
00:04:52,469 --> 00:04:55,739
an average can hide date,
citation or routing problems.

88
00:04:55,999 --> 00:04:58,168
Row two scored zero on Task Adherence:

89
00:04:58,168 --> 00:05:01,897
the answer never applied the payment
date to the refund deadline.

90
00:05:02,157 --> 00:05:06,461
Row six scored three on Relevance:
it never said which credit tier applies.

91
00:05:06,721 --> 00:05:12,227
Row eleven, the GPU-menu question, scored
two: it only said to contact support.

92
00:05:12,487 --> 00:05:16,294
These trace back to v1's own rules
against date and amount reasoning.

93
00:05:16,554 --> 00:05:20,720
Keep honest uncertainty; never rewrite
a saved response to look correct.

94
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:25,145
In Agent Optimizer, select
v1 and the same dev12,

95
00:05:25,145 --> 00:05:28,763
optimize instructions only,
limit candidates to two,

96
00:05:28,763 --> 00:05:32,616
and assign separate optimization
and evaluation models.

97
00:05:32,876 --> 00:05:34,722
The job succeeded in twelve minutes.

98
00:05:34,982 --> 00:05:39,426
Its internal score rose
from 0.844 to 0.865.

99
00:05:39,686 --> 00:05:44,302
But the raw candidate kept v1's
never-rules and copied dev12 values,

100
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:47,645
like document IDs
and a 94 percent credit mapping.

101
00:05:47,905 --> 00:05:50,174
That is memorization, not improvement.

102
00:05:50,434 --> 00:05:52,917
Review the changes, remove dev12 facts,

103
00:05:52,917 --> 00:05:55,985
and replace prohibitions
with general guidance.

104
00:05:56,245 --> 00:05:59,309
The internal 0-to-1 score
is not a managed-evaluation

105
00:05:59,309 --> 00:06:01,040
score or production approval.

106
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,713
Create v2 only from a reviewed candidate;

107
00:06:04,713 --> 00:06:08,669
here the operator removed dev12
facts and wrote general guidance.

108
00:06:08,929 --> 00:06:14,207
Add its run to the same evaluation, with
identical dataset, evaluators and Judge.

109
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:16,656
All twelve rows completed without errors.

110
00:06:16,916 --> 00:06:23,629
Eleven passed both criteria, up from nine;
mean Relevance rose from 3.75 to 4.58.

111
00:06:23,889 --> 00:06:26,797
In Compare runs, with v1 as baseline,

112
00:06:26,797 --> 00:06:31,676
Relevance improved by 0.83;
Task Adherence is inconclusive.

113
00:06:31,936 --> 00:06:36,316
Row eleven still fails: the GPU-menu
question cannot be verified.

114
00:06:36,576 --> 00:06:39,804
This is evidence on twelve
rows, not production approval.

115
00:06:40,064 --> 00:06:41,577
Do not promote or publish.

116
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,233
The last step is not
unconditional deletion.

117
00:06:45,493 --> 00:06:48,419
This run explicitly
retains the resource group,

118
00:06:48,419 --> 00:06:50,632
so no deletion command was executed.

119
00:06:50,892 --> 00:06:55,417
The group still exists with six resources:
the Foundry account and project,

120
00:06:55,417 --> 00:06:59,448
Search, Application Insights,
the log workspace and an alert rule.

121
00:06:59,708 --> 00:07:03,373
Retention keeps incurring charges,
including Search and logs.

122
00:07:03,633 --> 00:07:06,386
Deletion needs a separate,
explicit approval;

123
00:07:06,386 --> 00:07:10,241
closing a browser or deleting local
records does not stop billing.

124
00:07:10,501 --> 00:07:12,409
Keep the private configuration,

125
00:07:12,409 --> 00:07:15,679
ownership manifest and identifiers
needed to reopen it.

126
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,133
You can now reopen
the retained environment:

127
00:07:20,133 --> 00:07:24,498
the guide, the lab-en-v14
folder, the Agent lab-en-v14-iq,

128
00:07:24,498 --> 00:07:27,408
and dataset lab-en-dev12, version one.

129
00:07:27,668 --> 00:07:32,149
Use the recorded names and versions, not
results from another account or dataset.

130
00:07:32,409 --> 00:07:36,460
The point is not one high score,
but inspecting actual answers and reasons

131
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:40,576
under fixed conditions and adopting
only justified instruction changes.

132
00:07:40,836 --> 00:07:43,023
Correct procedural errors in the reusable

133
00:07:43,023 --> 00:07:45,331
guide without inserting
this run's results.

134
00:07:45,591 --> 00:07:48,083
This video is a separate
execution summary;

135
00:07:48,083 --> 00:07:52,796
finishing the lab grants no production
approval and guarantees no future quality.
